Security audit (module: license — backend/src/lib/license.ts):
  Threat model: revoke-list bypass, license forgery, time-of-check
  vs time-of-use.

  Re-read confirmed:
  - Verification is offline ed25519 with embedded pubkey; no
    network trust path.
  - Revoke-list is fetched from FileServer with 5-min cache, bound
    to specific customerId. A revoked license fails fast even if
    the file itself signs ok.
  - readLicenseFromDisk is the only entry point; license body is
    parsed JSON-first then signature-verified, so a malformed
    license fails BEFORE any field is trusted.
  - expiresAt comparison uses Date.now() with no skew tolerance —
    correct for license expiry (we WANT off-by-second to favor
    the protection side, not the holder).
  - Features array is read-only after parse; admin UI surfaces
    them via /api/admin/license but never writes back.

  No vulns. Pubkey shared with manifest-verify (already noted as
  MVP simplification in SECURITY_ARCHITECTURE.md §1).

